.TH STREMIO 1 "2026-09-16" "stremio" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
stremio \- GTK4/WebKitGTK6 desktop shell for Stremio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stremio
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIURI\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stremio
is a native GTK4 desktop application that embeds the Stremio web client
(via WebKitGTK6) alongside a local streaming server, providing a standalone
media center experience for movies, series and add-ons.
.PP
On startup it launches the streaming server itself, by running
.B node
on the script named by the
.B SERVER_PATH
environment variable, and points its embedded browser view at it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dev
Open the WebKit developer tools on startup.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-url =\fIURL\fR
Set the startup URL loaded in the embedded browser view. Defaults to the
local streaming server's web client proxy URL.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-window\-decorations
Disable client-side window decorations (title bar).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version number and exit.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I URI
An optional URI (e.g. a stream or magnet link) passed through to the
underlying GTK application for handling, the same way a file manager or
browser would hand off a link to a registered application.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/stremio/
Per-user application data directory, or
.I ~/.local/share/stremio/
when
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
is unset.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SERVER_PATH
Path to the streaming server script that is run with
.BR node .
Required: the application exits if it is unset.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for the per-user data directory described under
.BR FILES .
.SH AUTHOR
Smart Code OOD (Stremio).
.SH REPORTING BUGS
https://github.com/Stremio/stremio-linux-shell/issues
